PART 1

Read this first
What this actually is
Claude is not a video editor with buttons. What it does is write code that builds your video, then render that code to an MP4.

The engine is Remotion — a tool that makes videos out of React components, the same kind of code that makes websites. So a caption is not a text layer you drag, it is a line of code that says "show these words at 2.4 seconds, in SF Pro, on a black box at 93% opacity". A graphic is not a template, it is drawn fresh for your video.

That is the whole trick, and it is why the output does not look like a template:

Nothing is generic. Every animation is written for your line, at your timestamp, in your colours.
It scales. Once Claude knows your style, the fiftieth reel takes the same effort as the first.
It is repeatable. The edit is a file. You can change one number and re-render it a month later, exactly.

THE HONEST VERSION

You are not clicking a button. You are directing. You still watch the draft, tell Claude what feels off, and it fixes it — the same conversation you would have with a human editor, except this one works in code and never gets tired.

Your first reel will take a couple of hours, because you are learning what to ask for. After that it is roughly 20 to 40 minutes of your attention per reel.

