Interrupt whenever you like
You do not have to wait for Claude to finish. Click stop, or just type a correction and press Enter. If you see it heading the wrong way at second 4 of a 50-second reel, say so immediately instead of waiting for the render.


PART 3

The folder
This is the part that makes the whole thing work. Claude is good at editing when it knows where everything lives. Four subfolders, fixed names, and it never has to guess.

3.1  Build it
In Finder (or File Explorer), make a folder called AI Video Editor. Downloads is fine. Inside it, make four folders:

AI Video Editor/

├── Raw/          your trimmed footage

├── Reference/    your old reels — the style to copy

├── Resources/    music, logos, B-roll you already have

└── Export/       where the finished reel lands


Then go back to the Code tab, click the project folder control, choose Open folder…, and select AI Video Editor. That is the setup done — Claude can now see all four.

WHY THE NAMES MATTER

Keep these four names exactly as they are. Every prompt in this guide, and the skill in Part 6, refers to them. If you rename Reference to "Refs", you will have to explain that every single session.

3.2  Raw — your footage
One trimmed MP4 of you talking. Shot vertical, 9:16. Mine come straight off an iPhone with an external mic, so video and audio are one file — that is what Claude expects.

Trim it first. Cut false starts and retakes. Leave the good take only.
Leave the look-aways in. The parts where you turn to read your script off a screen — leave them. Claude keeps your audio and covers the picture with B-roll or a graphic. That is a feature, not a problem to fix.
Do not add captions or music yourself. Claude does both, and pre-burnt captions can never be removed.
4K is fine. Claude makes a smaller working copy to edit against, and goes back to the original for the final render.
3.3  Reference — your style
This is the folder people skip, and it is the one that decides whether the output looks like you or looks like AI.

Drop in 3 to 7 of your own past reels — the ones you were happy with. Claude watches them and pulls out your actual style: how fast you cut, where your captions sit, what your graphics look like, how your hook is paced.

You can also drop in a plain text file with links to other creators whose editing you want to borrow from. Claude cannot watch an Instagram link directly, so save the video itself into the folder, or screen-record 10 seconds of it and drop that in instead.

IF YOU ARE STARTING FROM ZERO

No past reels you like? Put in 3 to 5 reels from creators whose editing you admire, and say so in your prompt: "match the pacing and caption style of the references, but keep the colours in Resources." It works, and by reel three you will have your own references to swap in.

