5.10  Fonts, and one file that saves you repeating yourself
Claude uses the fonts already installed on your computer. I use SF Pro for captions and New York for the serif accents; both come from Apple's developer fonts page, free to download. Read Apple's licence before using them commercially — it is written around interface mock-ups. If you want a font with no questions attached, Inter from Google Fonts is free for anything and looks close.

Now the file that saves you the most time. Create CLAUDE.md in your AI Video Editor folder. Claude reads it automatically at the start of every session, so your setup and style live there permanently instead of being re-typed:

# My reel editing setup

 

## Machine

- Python video tools: ~/videotools/bin/python (rembg, sherpa-onnx, pocketsphinx)

- ffmpeg and ffprobe are on PATH

 

## My style — always

- 1080x1920, 30fps, H.264, CRF 16, AAC 320k

- Captions: SF Pro Display Bold, white, on a black box at 93% opacity

- Dark background #0A0A0A, one accent colour only

- Split screen: graphic on top, my face below, seam at y=940

- Never colour-grade my face. Never change my voice.

- Show me one still before any full render

 

## Folders

- Raw/ my footage · Reference/ my style · Resources/ my assets · Export/ output


Change the style lines to your own. This single file is the difference between a good first draft and three rounds of corrections.

